course: dictionary
lesson: 10602
title: Undigested
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undigested means not broken down yet. The prefix un- means not, and digest means to break food down so the body can use it. Spotting the parts inside a word is a useful way to work out what it means.
explain: «Poo is about three-quarters water, and much of the rest is bacteria, undigested fibre and old cells from the gut lining.» This tells us that some fibre is not broken down by the body, so it passes through still in its original form.
explain: The word also works for ideas. If you learn «undigested facts» by heart without understanding them, you have taken them in but not processed them yet. Ask yourself: have I really thought about this, or have I only memorised it?
fact: Undigested means not broken down by the body, or not understood properly yet.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so undigested means not digested.
fact: Some fibre passes through the body undigested.
fact: In school, facts learned by heart without understanding are sometimes called «undigested facts».
fact: «Undigested» is an adjective: it describes a noun, like undigested food or undigested facts.
exercise: Corn skins can pass through the body. What does undigested mean for them? | Chewed into small pieces | Turned into energy | Eaten twice | *Not broken down by the body
exercise: Maya has learned her spellings by heart but does not know what they mean. Her teacher says her learning is still undigested. What does that mean? | Written in pencil | Fully understood and remembered forever | Very hungry | *Not understood properly yet
exercise: The prefix in undigested is un-. What does un- mean? | *Not | Under | Very | Again
test: Which word from this lesson fits facts learned by heart without understanding? | *Undigested | Luminous | Curt | Ancient
test: Which sentence uses undigested correctly? | *Some seeds passed through the body undigested. | The river was undigested and fast. | The sun is undigested in the sky. | She ran undigested to the bus stop.
exam: In «undigested facts», what does undigested suggest? | Facts that are fully understood and remembered | *Facts that have been learned without really being understood yet | Facts that are very old | Facts written in a book
